{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DEaQZuKA3XHHw7tVJpxfpX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# loop-launcher.sh — the single almanac launcher (ralph + harden + converge).\n3\t#\n4\t# almanac_loop_launch <type> [native flags…] interactively configures and starts\n5\t# a loop run. It is loop-agnostic: one launcher for every consumer — `almanac\n6\t# ralph`, `almanac harden`, the hub's New-run flow, and the ralph skill launcher\n7\t# all route here, so the config UX is identical everywhere (the PRD's \"almanac\n8\t# launcher, not per-loop reimplementations\").\n9\t#\n10\t# Each loop's flag parsing, prompts, env-export, and runner exec live in its\n11\t# adapter (lib/loops/<name>.sh) as the `launch` verb, and its --help text as the\n12\t# `launch_usage` verb. The launcher dispatches via the loop-adapter seam — no\n13\t# central case-statement branches on loop type, so adding a 4th loop is a\n14\t# single new file in lib/loops/.\n15\t#\n16\t# The shared bits — field collectors (provider / choice / positive-int) and the\n17\t# summary panel — stay here because every adapter uses them identically. They\n18\t# are sourced once at launcher boot, so any adapter dispatched through\n19\t# `almanac_loop_launch` finds them in scope.\n20\t#\n21\t# Requires lib/core.sh (_die/_info/_success), sourced by every entry point before\n22\t# this file. The gum-or-plain UI seam (almanac_loop_ui_*) lives in lib/ui.sh and\n23\t# is pulled in directly below, so the launcher's dependency on it is explicit.\n24\t\n25\t# The launcher drives the whole config UX through the gum-or-plain seam\n26\t# (choose/input/confirm/render). Source it directly and idempotently so the\n27\t# dependency is the launcher's own, not borrowed from whatever sourced this file.\n28\tif ! declare -F almanac_loop_ui_choose >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n29\t  __loop_launcher_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n30\t  # shellcheck source=lib/ui.sh\n31\t  source \"$__loop_launcher_dir/ui.sh\"\n32\t  unset __loop_launcher_dir\n33\tfi\n34\t\n35\t# Provider knowledge (availability, the model/effort menus, default-selection,\n36\t# the provider list) lives in the provider-adapter seam (lib/agent.sh →\n37\t# almanac_provider_*). The launcher consumes it rather than branching on provider\n38\t# name. Source it directly and idempotently so the dependency is the launcher's\n39\t# own, not borrowed from whatever sourced this file.\n40\tif ! declare -F almanac_provider_default >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n41\t  __loop_launcher_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n42\t  # shellcheck source=lib/agent.sh\n43\t  source \"$__loop_launcher_dir/agent.sh\"\n44\t  unset __loop_launcher_dir\n45\tfi\n46\t\n47\t# The loop-adapter seam (almanac_loop_adapter_*) lives in lib/loops.sh. The\n48\t# launcher dispatches the `launch` verb through it (each loop adapter owns its\n49\t# own config UI + exec). Source it directly and idempotently so the dependency\n50\t# is the launcher's own, not borrowed from whatever sourced this file.\n51\tif ! declare -F almanac_loop_adapter_call >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n52\t  __loop_launcher_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n53\t  # shellcheck source=lib/loops.sh\n54\t  source \"$__loop_launcher_dir/loops.sh\"\n55\t  unset __loop_launcher_dir\n56\tfi\n57\t\n58\t# --- field collectors ---------------------------------------------------------\n59\t#\n60\t# Used by every loop adapter's `launch` verb (lib/loops/<name>.sh::almanac_loop_<name>_launch)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2788a3dc-ec0d-4660-89bb-3c9bc3797157","uuid":"b555f1b6-c87d-4fbd-ac14-7b456dd3adfc","timestamp":"2026-05-26T14:56:58.079Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/lib/loop-launcher.sh","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# loop-launcher.sh — the single almanac launcher (ralph + harden + converge).\n#\n# almanac_loop_launch <type> [native flags…] interactively configures and starts\n# a loop run. It is loop-agnostic: one launcher for every consumer — `almanac\n# ralph`, `almanac harden`, the hub's New-run flow, and the ralph skill launcher\n# all route here, so the config UX is identical everywhere (the PRD's \"almanac\n# launcher, not per-loop reimplementations\").\n#\n# Each loop's flag parsing, prompts, env-export, and runner exec live in its\n# adapter (lib/loops/<name>.sh) as the `launch` verb, and its --help text as the\n# `launch_usage` verb. The launcher dispatches via the loop-adapter seam — no\n# central case-statement branches on loop type, so adding a 4th loop is a\n# single new file in lib/loops/.\n#\n# The shared bits — field collectors (provider / choice / positive-int) and the\n# summary panel — stay here because every adapter uses them identically. They\n# are sourced once at launcher boot, so any adapter dispatched through\n# `almanac_loop_launch` finds them in scope.\n#\n# Requires lib/core.sh (_die/_info/_success), sourced by every entry point before\n# this file. The gum-or-plain UI seam (almanac_loop_ui_*) lives in lib/ui.sh and\n# is pulled in directly below, so the launcher's dependency on it is explicit.\n\n# The launcher drives the whole config UX through the gum-or-plain seam\n# (choose/input/confirm/render). Source it directly and idempotently so the\n# dependency is the launcher's own, not borrowed from whatever sourced this file.\nif ! declare -F almanac_loop_ui_choose >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  __loop_launcher_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n  # shellcheck source=lib/ui.sh\n  source \"$__loop_launcher_dir/ui.sh\"\n  unset __loop_launcher_dir\nfi\n\n# Provider knowledge (availability, the model/effort menus, default-selection,\n# the provider list) lives in the provider-adapter seam (lib/agent.sh →\n# almanac_provider_*). The launcher consumes it rather than branching on provider\n# name. Source it directly and idempotently so the dependency is the launcher's\n# own, not borrowed from whatever sourced this file.\nif ! declare -F almanac_provider_default >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  __loop_launcher_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n  # shellcheck source=lib/agent.sh\n  source \"$__loop_launcher_dir/agent.sh\"\n  unset __loop_launcher_dir\nfi\n\n# The loop-adapter seam (almanac_loop_adapter_*) lives in lib/loops.sh. The\n# launcher dispatches the `launch` verb through it (each loop adapter owns its\n# own config UI + exec). Source it directly and idempotently so the dependency\n# is the launcher's own, not borrowed from whatever sourced this file.\nif ! declare -F almanac_loop_adapter_call >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  __loop_launcher_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n  # shellcheck source=lib/loops.sh\n  source \"$__loop_launcher_dir/loops.sh\"\n  unset __loop_launcher_dir\nfi\n\n# --- field collectors ---------------------------------------------------------\n#\n# Used by every loop adapter's `launch` verb (lib/loops/<name>.sh::almanac_loop_<name>_launch).","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":161}}}
