{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JrCsbrdfxRkMjbiRb1ZRjh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# lib/agent.sh — the agent/provider seam.\n3\t#\n4\t# Per the module map, lib/agent.sh owns \"the three shapes + provider dispatch\".\n5\t# Two layers live here:\n6\t#   1. The provider-adapter seam (loop-engine-split slice 03): discovery of\n7\t#      lib/providers/<name>.sh, contract dispatch (callers never branch on a\n8\t#      provider name), and the single default-selection policy.\n9\t#   2. The three agent-run shapes (slice 04): almanac_loop_agent_capture /\n10\t#      _stream / _raw — intention-revealing replacements for the old\n11\t#      mode-parametric almanac_loop_agent_run. Each takes only what its shape\n12\t#      needs (no invalid mode combinations to guard); they consume the adapter's\n13\t#      argv + filter and own ONLY execution mechanics (exec, capture, stream,\n14\t#      PIPESTATUS exit threading).\n15\t#\n16\t# Self-contained: the seam uses only printf / command -v / source. The run shapes\n17\t# add jq / tee / grep / mktemp (coreutils) and emit diagnostics through _error\n18\t# when a caller has sourced lib/core.sh, falling back to a plain stderr line\n19\t# otherwise (_almanac_agent_err) — so there is still no hard dependency on\n20\t# lib/core.sh and any caller (or test) can source this file directly. Provider\n21\t# adapters are auto-loaded at source time (almanac_provider_load below).\n22\t\n23\t__almanac_agent_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n24\t\n25\t# Normalise a provider name to its adapter key (lowercase; claude-code → claude).\n26\talmanac_provider_key() {\n27\t  local k\n28\t  k=\"$(printf '%s' \"$1\" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')\"\n29\t  case \"$k\" in\n30\t    claude-code) k=\"claude\" ;;\n31\t  esac\n32\t  printf '%s' \"$k\"\n33\t}\n34\t\n35\t# Source every provider adapter (idempotent — adapters only define functions).\n36\talmanac_provider_load() {\n37\t  local f\n38\t  for f in \"$__almanac_agent_dir\"/providers/*.sh; do\n39\t    [ -f \"$f\" ] || continue\n40\t    # shellcheck source=/dev/null\n41\t    source \"$f\"\n42\t  done\n43\t  return 0\n44\t}\n45\t\n46\t# List discovered provider names — the provider list IS the files present, so\n47\t# there is no second place to update. Sorted by the glob (alphabetical).\n48\talmanac_provider_list() {\n49\t  local f name\n50\t  for f in \"$__almanac_agent_dir\"/providers/*.sh; do"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2788a3dc-ec0d-4660-89bb-3c9bc3797157","uuid":"9109707a-0571-4dd5-9686-b415bd21285d","timestamp":"2026-05-26T14:58:29.761Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/lib/agent.sh","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# lib/agent.sh — the agent/provider seam.\n#\n# Per the module map, lib/agent.sh owns \"the three shapes + provider dispatch\".\n# Two layers live here:\n#   1. The provider-adapter seam (loop-engine-split slice 03): discovery of\n#      lib/providers/<name>.sh, contract dispatch (callers never branch on a\n#      provider name), and the single default-selection policy.\n#   2. The three agent-run shapes (slice 04): almanac_loop_agent_capture /\n#      _stream / _raw — intention-revealing replacements for the old\n#      mode-parametric almanac_loop_agent_run. Each takes only what its shape\n#      needs (no invalid mode combinations to guard); they consume the adapter's\n#      argv + filter and own ONLY execution mechanics (exec, capture, stream,\n#      PIPESTATUS exit threading).\n#\n# Self-contained: the seam uses only printf / command -v / source. The run shapes\n# add jq / tee / grep / mktemp (coreutils) and emit diagnostics through _error\n# when a caller has sourced lib/core.sh, falling back to a plain stderr line\n# otherwise (_almanac_agent_err) — so there is still no hard dependency on\n# lib/core.sh and any caller (or test) can source this file directly. Provider\n# adapters are auto-loaded at source time (almanac_provider_load below).\n\n__almanac_agent_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n\n# Normalise a provider name to its adapter key (lowercase; claude-code → claude).\nalmanac_provider_key() {\n  local k\n  k=\"$(printf '%s' \"$1\" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')\"\n  case \"$k\" in\n    claude-code) k=\"claude\" ;;\n  esac\n  printf '%s' \"$k\"\n}\n\n# Source every provider adapter (idempotent — adapters only define functions).\nalmanac_provider_load() {\n  local f\n  for f in \"$__almanac_agent_dir\"/providers/*.sh; do\n    [ -f \"$f\" ] || continue\n    # shellcheck source=/dev/null\n    source \"$f\"\n  done\n  return 0\n}\n\n# List discovered provider names — the provider list IS the files present, so\n# there is no second place to update. Sorted by the glob (alphabetical).\nalmanac_provider_list() {\n  local f name\n  for f in \"$__almanac_agent_dir\"/providers/*.sh; do","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":279}}}
