{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016iz6e21xGTauTreTtdSSGM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# harden-core.sh - Harden loop rubric bootstrap + reviewer helpers\n3\t\n4\t# loop-core.sh (the old shared-engine barrel) is deleted; harden-core sources the\n5\t# focused modules it actually uses, each directly and idempotently so it works\n6\t# both through bin/almanac and when a test sources this file directly. core.sh\n7\t# is sourced literally (it owns the helper); the other deps go through\n8\t# _almanac_source_sibling so the boilerplate stays minimal.\n9\tif ! declare -F _error >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n10\t  __harden_core_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n11\t  # shellcheck source=lib/core.sh\n12\t  source \"$__harden_core_dir/core.sh\"\n13\t  unset __harden_core_dir\n14\tfi\n15\t\n16\t# Explicit deps (each declared module is the contract surface this file consumes;\n17\t# transitive availability is not relied on).\n18\t_almanac_source_sibling agent.sh    almanac_loop_agent_capture   # agent run shapes (ratify/fixer)\n19\t_almanac_source_sibling run.sh      almanac_loop_register_run    # run registry + worker paths/health\n20\t_almanac_source_sibling worker.sh   almanac_loop_worker_start    # worker orchestration (reviewer/fixer fan-out)\n21\t_almanac_source_sibling ui.sh       almanac_loop_ui_render       # gum-or-plain dashboard seam\n22\t_almanac_source_sibling role.sh     almanac_loop_role_config     # per-role provider/model/effort resolution\n23\t_almanac_source_sibling feedback.sh almanac_loop_feedback_run    # objective fixer gate\n24\t\n25\t# --- Role config (per-role provider / model / effort) --------------------------"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2788a3dc-ec0d-4660-89bb-3c9bc3797157","uuid":"fb8ee06a-0abe-4969-9cd0-af605652e2df","timestamp":"2026-05-26T15:03:25.078Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/cod