{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ky7T33XAb7pN24d3iDVyg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# worker.sh — worker orchestration (background fan-out).\n3\t#\n4\t# Per CONTEXT.md's module map, this owns the WRITE/spawn side of a run's workers:\n5\t# write/mark a worker's status.tsv, spawn a provider run in the background\n6\t# (almanac_loop_worker_start — the fan-out), and stream one worker's live event\n7\t# log (almanac_loop_worker_watch). harden's reviewer/fixer fan-out is the\n8\t# consumer; the run-level registry, the worker PATH helpers + the worker-health\n9\t# read views live in lib/run.sh (this is the orchestration layer on top of them).\n10\t#\n11\t# Dependencies (sourced idempotently): lib/core.sh (_warn + the _almanac_source_sibling\n12\t# helper used below), lib/run.sh (worker path helpers + almanac_loop_status_field +\n13\t# almanac_loop_now_utc), lib/agent.sh (the capture shape the spawned worker runs).\n14\t# core.sh loads first via the literal snippet so the sibling helper is in scope.\n15\tif ! declare -F _warn >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n16\t  __worker_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n17\t  # shellcheck source=lib/core.sh\n18\t  source \"$__worker_dir/core.sh\"\n19\t  unset __worker_dir\n20\tfi\n21\t\n22\t_almanac_source_sibling run.sh   almanac_loop_worker_status_file\n23\t_almanac_source_sibling agent.sh almanac_loop_agent_capture\n24\t\n25\t# THE single source of truth for the worker-status schema: the canonical field\n26\t# list in write order. Mirrors run.sh's almanac_loop_record_fields; the generic\n27\t# almanac_loop_tsv_record_set engine iterates this list so every worker record\n28\t# carries the same keys regardless of which subset a caller supplies.\n29\talmanac_loop_worker_record_fields() {\n30\t  printf '%s\\n' \\"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2788a3dc-ec0d-4660-89bb-3c9bc3797157","uuid":"7943afd9-e5b3-448e-a3e5-de754a7affa1","timestamp":"2026-05-26T15:03:32.586Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/lib/worker.sh","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# worker.sh — worker orchestration (background fan-out).\n#\n# Per CONTEXT.md's module map, this owns the WRITE/spawn side of a run's workers:\n# write/mark a worker's status.tsv, spawn a provider run in the background\n# (almanac_loop_worker_start — the fan-out), and stream one worker's live event\n# log (almanac_loop_worker_watch). harden's reviewer/fixer fan-out is the\n# consumer; the run-level registry, the worker PATH helpers + the worker-health\n# read views live in lib/run.sh (this is the orchestration layer on top of them).\n#\n# Dependencies (sourced idempotently): lib/core.sh (_warn + the _almanac_source_sibling\n# helper used below), lib/run.sh (worker path helpers + almanac_loop_status_field +\n# almanac_loop_now_utc), lib/agent.sh (the capture shape the spawned worker runs).\n# core.sh loads first via the literal snippet so the sibling helper is in scope.\nif ! declare -F _warn >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  __worker_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n  # shellcheck source=lib/core.sh\n  source \"$__worker_dir/core.sh\"\n  unset __worker_dir\nfi\n\n_almanac_source_sibling run.sh   almanac_loop_worker_status_file\n_almanac_source_sibling agent.sh almanac_loop_agent_capture\n\n# THE single source of truth for the worker-status schema: the canonical field\n# list in write order. Mirrors run.sh's almanac_loop_record_fields; the generic\n# almanac_loop_tsv_record_set engine iterates this list so every worker record\n# carries the same keys regardless of which subset a caller supplies.\nalmanac_loop_worker_record_fields() {\n  printf '%s\\n' \\","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":178}}}
