{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014frRPmZHQgakRWTnnNHu82","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# loop-launcher.sh — the single almanac launcher (ralph + harden + converge).\n3\t#\n4\t# almanac_loop_launch <type> [native flags…] interactively configures and starts\n5\t# a loop run. It is loop-agnostic: one launcher for every consumer — `almanac\n6\t# ralph`, `almanac harden`, the hub's New-run flow, and the ralph skill launcher\n7\t# all route here, so the config UX is identical everywhere (the PRD's \"almanac\n8\t# launcher, not per-loop reimplementations\").\n9\t#\n10\t# Each loop's flag parsing, prompts, env-export, and runner exec live in its\n11\t# adapter (lib/loops/<name>.sh) as the `launch` verb, and its --help text as the\n12\t# `launch_usage` verb. The launcher dispatches via the loop-adapter seam — no\n13\t# central case-statement branches on loop type, so adding a 4th loop is a\n14\t# single new file in lib/loops/.\n15\t#\n16\t# The shared bits — field collectors (provider / choice / positive-int) and the\n17\t# summary panel — stay here because every adapter uses them identically. They\n18\t# are sourced once at launcher boot, so any adapter dispatched through\n19\t# `almanac_loop_launch` finds them in scope.\n20\t#\n21\t# Requires lib/core.sh (_die/_info/_success + _almanac_source_sibling), sourced\n22\t# by every entry point before this file. The deps below are each declared\n23\t# explicitly through the sibling helper so the launcher's seam dependencies\n24\t# aren't borrowed from whatever sourced this file.\n25\t_almanac_source_sibling ui.sh    almanac_loop_ui_choose       # gum-or-plain UI seam\n26\t_almanac_source_sibling agent.sh almanac_provider_default     # provider-adapter seam (availability/default)\n27\t_almanac_source_sibling loops.sh almanac_loop_adapter_call    # loop-adapter dispatch\n28\t\n29\t# --- field collectors ---------------------------------------------------------\n30\t#\n31\t# Used by every loop adapter's `launch` verb (lib/loops/<name>.sh::almanac_loop_<name>_launch).\n32\t# The underscore prefix signals \"private to the launching subsystem (this file +\n33\t# adapter launch verbs)\" — not for callers outside that path.\n34\t\n35\t# Pick a provider into the named-by-$1 variable if it is empty. Lists only"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2788a3dc-ec0d-4660-89bb-3c9bc3797157","uuid":"68650eac-72d1-4c9a-ae81-99e07b57b485","timestamp":"2026-05-26T15:03:35.520Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/lib/loop-launcher.sh","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# loop-launcher.sh — the single almanac launcher (ralph + harden + converge).\n#\n# almanac_loop_launch <type> [native flags…] interactively configures and starts\n# a loop run. It is loop-agnostic: one launcher for every consumer — `almanac\n# ralph`, `almanac harden`, the hub's New-run flow, and the ralph skill launcher\n# all route here, so the config UX is identical everywhere (the PRD's \"almanac\n# launcher, not per-loop reimplementations\").\n#\n# Each loop's flag parsing, prompts, env-export, and runner exec live in its\n# adapter (lib/loops/<name>.sh) as the `launch` verb, and its --help text as the\n# `launch_usage` verb. The launcher dispatches via the loop-adapter seam — no\n# central case-statement branches on loop type, so adding a 4th loop is a\n# single new file in lib/loops/.\n#\n# The shared bits — field collectors (provider / choice / positive-int) and the\n# summary panel — stay here because every adapter uses them identically. They\n# are sourced once at launcher boot, so any adapter dispatched through\n# `almanac_loop_launch` finds them in scope.\n#\n# Requires lib/core.sh (_die/_info/_success + _almanac_source_sibling), sourced\n# by every entry point before this file. The deps below are each declared\n# explicitly through the sibling helper so the launcher's seam dependencies\n# aren't borrowed from whatever sourced this file.\n_almanac_source_sibling ui.sh    almanac_loop_ui_choose       # gum-or-plain UI seam\n_almanac_source_sibling agent.sh almanac_provider_default     # provider-adapter seam (availability/default)\n_almanac_source_sibling loops.sh almanac_loop_adapter_call    # loop-adapter dispatch\n\n# --- field collectors ---------------------------------------------------------\n#\n# Used by every loop adapter's `launch` verb (lib/loops/<name>.sh::almanac_loop_<name>_launch).\n# The underscore prefix signals \"private to the launching subsystem (this file +\n# adapter launch verbs)\" — not for callers outside that path.\n\n# Pick a provider into the named-by-$1 variable if it is empty. Lists only","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":132}}}
